From 247bf21e5eca760d2977274315bfc6498931f897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Michaud <jmichaud@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:19:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/23] [mya] Write dSYMs for MYA_HEAP builds on macOS Need the
 bug URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Build flags only. Debug macOS builds with MYA_HEAP on; nothing else changes.

Xcode: JavaScriptCore, WebCore, WebGPU and WebKit use
DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT = dwarf-with-dsym instead of dwarf when WK_MYA_HEAP
is YES. CMake: each shared library and executable target gets a POST_BUILD
dsymutil step that writes its dSYM where liblldb looks for it, next to the
image, or for a framework next to its bundle (Foo.framework.dSYM).

Why it is needed:
- Without a dSYM, liblldb reads debug info through the debug map, out of each
  .o file. Through the debug map it cannot find the compile unit that defines
  a global variable, so `SBTarget::FindGlobalVariables` comes back empty: the
  heap walk then has no type for any global or static (it reads every one as
  a root), and can find neither JSC's VM through `s_recentVM` nor WebCore's
  `g_commonVMOrNull` by type.
- With Xcode's compilation caching, an object file's debug info refers to its
  precompiled header's debug info inside the cache, which only dsymutil knows
  how to read. liblldb reading the .o files directly misses the types that
  only the prefix header's debug info describes (WebCore, WebGPU, WebKit).

Cost: dsymutil runs after every link of these images in MYA_HEAP builds,
which adds its time to each incremental build.

What we lose if it is not taken: on macOS, global variables have no types
(the DebugInfo tests that look them up fail) and heap walks of WebCore,
WebGPU and WebKit lose the types that come from prefix headers. Linux is
unaffected.

* Source/JavaScriptCore/Configurations/DebugRelease.xcconfig:
* Source/WebCore/Configurations/DebugRelease.xcconfig:
* Source/WebGPU/Configurations/DebugRelease.xcconfig:
* Source/WebKit/Configurations/DebugRelease.xcconfig:
* Source/cmake/WebKitMacros.cmake:

